      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Fall back after generated YouTube candidates fail**\n\nFor a multi-resource FanHub item whose primary YouTube video is removed but not yet marked `unavailable`, this treats its synthesized thumbnail URLs as renderable and selects it ahead of a secondary resource with valid artwork. When both generated URLs fail, `RecordThumbnail` only exhausts that selected resource's source list and never advances to the secondary resource, so the card still loses usable artwork during the exact unverified-failure interval this change handles. Fresh evidence in this revision is the new runtime failure path, which increments only a per-resource candidate index; fallback therefore needs to span resources rather than relying solely on candidates being syntactically constructible.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
